{"type":"assistant","uuid":"c7c4703b-2969-48da-b194-fee212c3a081","session_id":"ac363d40-4824-4eb9-9e84-f2187f26399e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"c7c4703b-2969-48da-b194-fee212c3a081","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Activities/IntroScreenActivity.java`\n\n### Root Cause\n\nTwo related issues in the `AuthenticationFragment` class:\n\n1. **Wrong encryption method text on slide 3**: The default auth method was `PASSWORD` while the default encryption type was `KEYSTORE`. The callback `onEncryptionChanged` only fired when the user *changed* the selection, so if the user never touched the dropdown, the third slide showed the wrong encryption method description.\n\n2. **\"Please set a password\" shown for Android KeyStore**: The adapter correctly disabled `PASSWORD`/`PIN` options when `KEYSTORE` encryption was selected, but the default auth selection was still `PASSWORD`. This caused `canGoForward()` to demand a password that the user couldn't select, creating a contradictory state.\n\n### Fix (2 changes)\n\n1. **Changed default auth method from `PASSWORD` to `NONE`**: This ensures navigation always works on the third slide regardless of which encryption type is selected, aligning with the UI text that states auth is optional for Android KeyStore.\n\n2. **Refactored adapter `isEnabled`/`getDropDownView`**: When `KEYSTORE` encryption is selected, all auth methods (including `NONE` and `DEVICE`) are now enabled. Previously, only `PASSWORD` and `PIN` were allowed regardless of encryption type, causing the contradiction.\n\nThe patch is saved to: `IntroScreenActivity.patch`"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56310,"output_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":54912,"total_tokens":56670}}}
